<title>USA: Fed adds reserves through overnight system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves through overnight system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added reserves to the banking system on Wednesday through overnight system repurchase agreements, the New York Fed confirmed.</p>
<p>The operation was expected, and analysts estimated the size at around $5.0 billion.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-7/16 percent, just below the 5-1/2 percent target rate.</p>
<p>(( -- Steven Scheer, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867 ))</p>
